https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-12353-4

| **Factor**                      | **Ahmed (2024)** – *Applied Computational Intelligence & Soft Computing*                                     | **Boujmiraz et al. (2026)** – *Computers and Education: AI*                                        | **Ahmed, Wani, Hammad et al. (2025)** – *Scientific Reports*                                                                     |
| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Type of Study**               | Original research                                                                                            | Systematic literature review (PRISMA)                                                              | Original research                                                                                                                |
| **Dataset**                     | Real institutional data from Wollo University, Kombolcha Institute of Technology (2017–2022 student records) | 281 records screened → 72 studies retained (2017–2024) from ScienceDirect, IEEE Xplore, Scopus     | Two Kaggle datasets: (1) 10,000 rows / 6 features; (2) 6,607 rows / 20 features                                                  |
| **Methods / Algorithms Used**   | K-Means clustering (Davies-Bouldin) + KNN, SVM, Decision Trees, Naïve Bayes                                  | Reviews ML + DL methods used across studies; no new model proposed                                 | 9 regressors: Linear, Ridge, KNN, SVR, RF, Bagging, XGBoost, CatBoost, AdaBoost + proposed Ensemble Voting Regressor             |
| **Key Factors / Features**      | Gender, region, entrance result, number of previous attempts, studied credits, disability                    | Demographic, behavioral, psychological, and socioeconomic factors                                  | Study hours, previous scores, sleep hours, extracurriculars, papers practiced, attendance, parental involvement, teacher quality |
| **Best-Performing Model**       | **SVM** achieved the highest accuracy among compared classifiers                                             | N/A — systematic review; notes Decision Trees and rule-based methods as common strong predictors   | **Ensemble Voting Regressor** — R² = 0.989 (Dataset 1), R² = 0.77 (Dataset 2)                                                    |
| **Explainability (XAI)**        | Not addressed                                                                                                | Central theme; highlights limited adoption of XAI despite its importance for pedagogical decisions | Uses **SHAP + LIME**; Previous Scores identified as the most influential feature (~62% contribution)                             |
| **Evaluation Metrics**          | Accuracy comparison across classifiers                                                                       | N/A — qualitative/systematic review                                                                | MAE, RMSE, R², 10-fold cross-validation, paired t-tests                                                                          |
| **Gap / Limitation Identified** | Does not explore deep learning; small regional dataset limits generalizability                               | Limited studies connect ML/DL predictions with actual explainability and interpretability          | Feature selection sometimes reduced performance; deep learning not tested; socioeconomic/psychological features not included     |
| **Future Work Suggested**       | Expand dataset scope and try additional algorithms                                                           | Encourage wider adoption of XAI in educational predictive models                                   | Explore deep learning/transformers, add socioeconomic factors, and develop real-time adaptive learning systems                   |
